A||N||8||fastback87||Auto Tranny problem on 87 GT||||5||
Z||000000||fastback87||11-18-2001||03:48 PM||||what would cause my tranny to engage into drive reeeeeaaaaal hard?  It seems to shift good between gears and into reverse but it feels like the engine is jumping out of the cradle when I put it in drive.  LMK.  Thanks you guys and gals are the best.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||11-18-2001||03:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fastback87:<BR><B>what would cause my tranny to engage into drive reeeeeaaaaal hard?  It seems to shift good between gears and into reverse but it feels like the engine is jumping out of the cradle when I put it in drive.  LMK.  Thanks you guys and gals are the best.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Line pressure too high? Give the tranny a new filter + fluid . <P>DON'T FLUSH unless you want to change the tranny in 6 months<P>||||reg||7
Z||000002||theogre||11-18-2001||04:21 PM||||a fairly large number of things can cause that.... Only 3 of them are under you control without ripping the tranny apart.<P>check all the motor/tranny mounts.<P>check/change the fluid.<P>check/adjust the TV cable.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_24||11-18-2001||04:28 PM||||Mach10 you said, DON'T FLUSH unless you want to change the tranny in 6 months.  Why not flush?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||5
Z||000004||fastback87||11-18-2001||04:58 PM||||allready have changed the tranny fluid and the filter, I used fully synthetic dextron 3.<P>What happens if the TV cable is too loose, or too tight?  I have adjusted the cable many times and it doesn't seem to adjust correctly.  I used the same procedure as the hanes manual tells.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||11-18-2001||05:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero_24:<BR><B>Mach10 you said, DON'T FLUSH unless you want to change the tranny in 6 months.  Why not flush?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>for some reason, at's seem to self-destruct soon after. not sure why, but i suspect that the pressure of the fluid blasting through the passages knocks it out of whack. not to mention potential loss of friction material from clutches... read: i don't know. just what i've seen.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||lou||11-18-2001||05:47 PM||||If it has a delay when you first put it in drive then I had the same problem, 87 gt 2.8. I changed the filter & fluid: same problem. Then I removed the valve body and cleaned it out, replaced the gasket and it worked fine.  If one of the axles moves as you are putting the car in gear from park then it is the differential and you need to rebuilt or replace the tranny.||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||11-18-2001||09:43 PM||||It sounds to me like a shot motor mount and/or dogbone (upper engine strut) -- the Throttle Valve cable will adjust the shift points (earlier or later) - to adjust it a notch toward the throttle body will resilt in a quicker shift and a notch away from the throttle body will resilt in a slower shift.<P>remove the TV cable and depress the adjustment button and move the slide all the way back into the cable housing. Hook up the cable and move the throttle full open by hand - the TV cable will adjust itself. I ususally then pull it out one more notch toward the throttle body for the proper shift points.<P>If you are still having problems, hook up with Boilermaker (on this Forum) - he is located in Greenwood - he knows how to adjust it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg">  <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A><p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 11-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||SKIDMARK||11-18-2001||10:49 PM||||Are you sure it's not the engine idle? First rule of AT's is make sure the engine is running right. If the idle is just a little too high it will slam into gear. The TV cable will not change the way it goes into gear from park or neutral. Like mentioned above, check all mounts including the dog-bone.||||reg||1
